 "description": "A price list and its corrigendum are a document set: the corrigendum is a reference at set position 1. With the replace check, the corrigendum row of B-200 replaces the price list row, and the unique check then finds B-200 one time. The corrigendum row of D-400 changes a row that the price list does not have, so it is SET_REPLACES_NOTHING. The two rows of C-300 in the price list are SET_DUPLICATE. A corrigendum row without its price is RECORD_MEMBER_MISSING, and a row with a code from the price list and a price from the corrigendum is RECORD_SOURCE_MIXED and takes no part in the checks (#613).",
